{"dog":{"age_group":"adult","application_url":"https://petstablished.com/public/search/redirect?application_type=adoption&pet_id=2502562&premium=true","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Medium mixed breed","breed_primary":"Mixed Breed","description_text":"Do senior dogs have your heart? They have ours too!\n\nTourmie may look like a young pup with her bright brown coat and floppy ears but she is a well seasoned and sultry 10 year old lady.\n\nWith a decade of lived experience, Tourmie wants nothing more than to spend her days laying around leisurely, sitting on park benches with her humans, being invited to picnics and even having sleepovers with famil and friends when her people need to travel!\n\nOn leash, Tourmie is an all star and every once in a while she'll cosplay as a spring chicken and become excited to see other dogs - don't let he full you though, she actually prefers to spend her golden years being a families one and only.\n\nTourmie also loves everyone she meets including human strangers and young children. Tourmie is extremely respectful, gentle and indepedent understand when its time to be involved and when it's time to not be the center of attention.\n\nTourmie may call out to you for a few minutes when left alone and once she realizes you are always coming back for her she settles quickly. Truly, all Tourmie wants to remind you when you leave is how much she values spending time with you and how eager she is to have you back home. When you do return home - Tourmie will always become your built in bestie always aspiring to be your shadow!\n\nOverall, Tourmie is an extremely low maintenancfe, easy going, snuggling and housebroken girl who spends her days not turning away from any treats offered and looks forward to spending her evenings cuddling in bed.\n\nLast year, Tourmie was found to have a malignant tumor however her prognosis remaings good! If you take the time to meet Tourmie, you will see for youself that she still has alot of 